      "writtenOn": "2023-10-04T10:20:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The use case we want to support here are\n1. Exist Incoming call \u003d\u003e Press the Answer/End call button will send hook-swtich\u003d1 to app\n  \n  mapping to `release_active_accept_held_impl`\n\n2. Exist Incoming call \u003d\u003e Press the Answer/End call twice button will send hook-swtich\u003d0 to app\n\n  mapping to `release_held_impl`\n3. No Exist Incoming call \u003d\u003e Press the Answer/End call button will send hook-swtich\u003d0 to app\n  \n  mapping to `hangup_call_impl`\n\n4. No Exist Incoming call \u003d\u003e Press the Answer/End call button twice should have no action.\n\n  should ignore this\n\nHold (2 secs) the Answer/End call button should always remain no function here. We are not support hold/resume in this stage.\n\nMay you help check whether this is current behavior?",
